 Changes & Voting Matters","url":"https://cdn.yahoofinance.com/prod/sec-filings/0001166691/000116669125000041/cmcsa-20250822.htm"}],"wiki":{"en":{"t":"Comcast","x":"Comcast Corporation, formerly known as Comcast Holdings, is an American multinational mass media, telecommunications, and entertainment conglomerate. Comcast's corporate headquarters is at the Comcast Center in Philadelphia, while NBCUniversal, Comcast's New York operations and other major Comcast assets are headquartered at 30 Rockefeller Plaza in Midtown Manhattan in New York City. The company was ranked 51st in the Forbes Global 2000 in 2023. It is the fourth-largest telecommunications company by worldwide revenue, after AT&T, Verizon, and China Mobile. Comcast is the third-largest pay-TV company, the second-largest cable TV company by subscribers, and the largest home Internet service provider in the United States.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comcast"},"ru":{"t":"Comcast","x":"Comcast Corporation, «Комкаст корпорейшн» — американская телекоммуникационная корпорация. Состоит из трёх основных подразделений, Comcast Cable, NBCUniversal и Sky. Является крупнейшим оператором кабельного телевидения и широкополосного доступа к интернету в США, а также крупнейшим оператором платного телевидения в мире с 52 млн абонентов.","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comcast"}},"wiki_at":"2026-10-15T14:02:00.451478+00:00"}